rowhammer (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A piece that comes to rest reaching into the hidden spawn rows above
    the field now ends the round (user report). Until now the only
    top-out the game knew was a blocked spawn position, so a piece could
    settle on the topmost row sticking out above it and the round simply
    went on - the field is 20 rows, and nothing that stays above them
    belongs to it.
  * The check runs after the line clear: a piece that pokes out but takes
    rows with it pulls the stack back down into the field, and that
    clutch move is rewarded rather than punished. An Ultra run that
    reaches its target with that very piece counts as won as well.
  * In the Hochwasser mode a rise that pushes the stack out of the field
    ends the round by the same rule - one row earlier than the previous
    check, which only refused to shift a cell off the board entirely.
  * Working rule recorded in CLAUDE.md: every change that concerns the
    multiplayer mode is work on version 2.x.x.

