rowhammer (0.51.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Marathon highscore list is stored in "highscore-marathon" from
    now on (user request). It was the only list without its mode in the
    file name - a leftover from the time when it was the only list there
    was - while highscore-ultra, highscore-sprint, highscore-timeattack
    and highscore-flood all name theirs.
  * An existing "highscore" file is renamed once at startup (mv), so no
    top ten is lost over a name: nothing about the file's content
    changes. The rename runs before --reset, which works from the file
    names the modules own and would otherwise report the file as absent
    and leave it behind. A target file that is already there is never
    overwritten; a failing rename is a hard error, because the data
    directory is then unwritable anyway.
  * --help, the manual and the README name the new file.

