rowhammer (0.44.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Retuned the wonder goals (user decision): every entry of WONDER_COSTS
    was multiplied by 100, so a wonder now costs 10000 to 640000 weighted
    rows instead of 100 to 6400 - 1270000 rows for all seven instead of
    12700. The old figures were scaled down for single-machine play and
    turned out far too cheap; the new ones are in the order of magnitude
    of the original (2500 to 500000 lines per wonder), where finishing a
    wonder is a long-term goal again. The doubling per wonder and the
    wonder sequence itself are unchanged.
  * The wonder page of the manual ("Anleitung") widened its cost column
    to six digits so the larger numbers keep their column.
  * Note for existing savegames: the banked row total is untouched, but
    it now buys less progress, so the construction site falls back to an
    earlier wonder and build stage.

