rowhammer (0.34.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the "Ultra" game mode (user request): the singleplayer menu now
    picks a mode, and Ultra is a race - clear ULTRA_TARGET_ROWS (150)
    rows of credit as fast as possible. The run ends the moment the
    target is reached and its play time is the result. Weighted rows are
    what counts, not physical lines, so the gold and silver squares are
    the short way to the goal (see CLAUDE.md 3.6).
  * Track the mode per round in GAME_MODE, kept across suspending a
    round into the main menu and across a restart from the end-of-round
    screen, so a resumed or restarted Ultra run stays an Ultra run.
  * Show the target and the rows still missing in the left HUD pane
    while an Ultra run is going ("Goal"/"Left", two of the pane's free
    rows); a normal round leaves them free as before.
  * Report the outcome in the box over the board: "ULTRA CLEAR" with the
    run's time (MM:SS.mmm) and its Ultra rank, or - for a run that
    topped out early - how far it got instead of a rank.
  * Store finished Ultra runs in their own top-ten list,
    <data-dir>/highscore-ultra, ordered by time with millisecond
    resolution (fastest first). A timed run and an endless round cannot
    be compared by rows, and a 150-row sprint must not displace the
    endless list's top ten. Only runs that reached the target are
    recorded; the rows of a failed attempt still build the wonders and
    feed the statistics like any other aborted round.

